From 24c0240427c6b55ce00527bce934029a95dadf82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 16:53:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 483/572] fix: use #ifdef PLAT_RO_XLAT_TABLES

PLAT_RO_XLAT_TABLES is only defined without a value, it should be
checked with `#ifdef`.
This corrects -Wundef GCC warnings.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 5e07093676550eef08c02d7efb56f81716dd4962 fix: use #ifdef PLAT_RO_XLAT_TABLES]
Change-Id: I239389fad4d41208f4a46cc446b18173794bd193
Signed-off-by: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/572123
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Tested-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
---
 include/common/bl_common.ld.h                    | 4 ++--
 include/lib/xlat_tables/xlat_tables_v2.h         | 4 ++--
